WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:03.310
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here.

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:07.460
After the release of the spectacular Avengers
Infinity War trailer, we've finally got a

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:10.670
much better look at what the Avengers will
be facing up to when Thanos and his Black

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.490
Order invade the Earth.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:16.840
And now some amazing descriptions from Infinity
War Lego sets have leaked that may reveal

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:20.369
what we can expect from six key action scenes
in the movie.

00:00:20.369 --> 00:00:24.769
My superhero giveaway is also running on this
video for all my subscribers and I'll have

00:00:24.769 --> 00:00:26.820
full details on that later in the video.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:31.649
And just before I go any further, obviously
I'm talking potential spoilers and speculation

00:00:31.649 --> 00:00:35.620
for the upcoming Avengers: Infinity War movie,
plus previous Marvel films.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.469
So, if you prefer, you can tap in the top
right to watch my breakdown of the official

00:00:39.469 --> 00:00:41.480
trailer instead.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:45.530
Let's get into the details of these six key
scenes which come from the release of Lego

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:48.540
set descriptions published on a toy site called
Exoforce.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:53.250
I'm going to start with a particularly interesting
set called "The Search For Thor's Weapon"

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:57.179
which includes minifigures for Thor, Rocket
Racoon and Groot and which also mentions an

00:00:57.179 --> 00:00:58.800
unknown infinity stone.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.920
The set describes a quest where Thor goes
off with Rocket and Groot in search of a new

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:05.390
weapon, now that he no longer has Mjolnir.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:09.330
Curiously, this description fits in with a
piece of official concept art that Marvel

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:13.690
released in a very early Infinity War teaser
video of Thor wielding what looks like an

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:16.470
axe and Rocket firing alongside him.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:21.620
The Lego set description also states that
Thor travels to a red planet called Nidavellir,

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:22.800
one of the Nine Realms.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.720
This planet which is inhabited by dwarves
is actually where Mjolnir was originally forged,

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.630
in the words of Odin, 'in the heart of a dying
star'.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:34.990
The leaked description mentions that Thor
using "space forges", which I think explains

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:38.970
this mysterious shot of Thor in the trailer
where he's straining to operate or control

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:40.690
some kind of machine.

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:45.250
An unspecified Infinity Stone is also mentioned
in the description, as well as using energy

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.000
to create a new axe.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.110
The axe referred to here is most likely Jarnbjorn,
a weapon forged by dwarves and used by Thor

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.490
before Mjolnir.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:57.840
The axe is incredibly sharp with the power
to slice through almost anything, and it's

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.450
also virtually indestructible.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:04.030
Based on the description, it also sounds like
an Infinity Stone might be involved in the

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:07.920
creation of Thor's new weapon and I think
this could be the Reality Stone, which we

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.700
last saw given to the Collector at the end
of Thor: The Dark World.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:15.690
We know from the Infinity War trailer that
Thanos already has the Power Stone and the

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:20.470
Space Stone; that his Black Order is extracting
the Mind Stone from Vision; and that Doctor

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.030
Strange has the Time Stone.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:26.730
And at the moment, I feel that the Soul Stone
is probably going to be in Wakanda.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:30.620
That leaves the Reality Stone, which was actually
mentioned in some recently leaked Infinity

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:35.000
War footage where Thanos interrogates the
Collector about an Infinity Stone, which Taneleer

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.319
Tivan claims he sold to someone.

00:02:37.319 --> 00:02:41.200
If what the Collector says is true, then I
wonder whether the person he sold it to might

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.400
be Peter Dinklage's character who then takes
it to the Dwarven home Nidavellir.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:51.210
The next set is based back on Earth with minifigures
of Bruce Banner, Falcon and Proxima Midnight,

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.570
plus the Soul Stone.

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:56.840
It describes a scene where Proxima Midnight
has captured a tower and starts firing on

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.670
a Hulkbuster Bruce Banner.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:03.010
This seems to confirm my theory from my trailer
breakdown video that it's not actually Tony

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:06.560
Stark we see in the Hulkbuster armour in the
Infinity War trailer.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:11.280
A six-limbed enemy is also mentioned in the
description, which means that the four-armed,

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.920
two-legged Outriders that the Black Order
commands will also be involved in this scene.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:20.340
Finally, the set description orders Falcon
to dive down and capture the Soul Stone, which

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:24.870
seems to confirm the final stone is being
kept in Wakanda, given that's where the trailer

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:27.459
shows the Hulkbuster.

00:03:27.459 --> 00:03:31.930
The epic battle in Wakanda, which we saw teased
in the trailer, also features in another set

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:36.680
that includes Captain America, Black Widow,
and an army of Outriders, as well as the Space

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:37.680
Stone.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:41.530
The set description talks about Captain America
and Black Widow helping in the defence of

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:43.640
Wakanda against the invading Outriders.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:48.260
Interestingly, it mentions that Cap uses his
shield in the battle, which confirms we will

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:52.890
be seeing Cap back with some kind of shield,
as we also heard Black Panther say in the

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:53.890
trailer.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:58.000
We know that Thanos will be after the Time
Stone, which at the end of Doctor Strange

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.069
was being stored in Strange's Sanctum Santorum.

00:04:01.069 --> 00:04:05.310
This Lego set description suggests that we'll
see Spider-Man and Iron Man join with Doctor

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:09.910
Strange to fend off two of Thanos's Black
Order, Cull Obsidian and Ebony Maw, during

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:12.030
their attack on the New York Sanctum.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:17.110
The fifth set reveals a potentially intriguing
moment involving Black Order member Corvus

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:20.099
Glaive, Vision, Black Panther and Shuri.

00:04:20.099 --> 00:04:24.529
It describes a scene where Corvus Glaive is
launching an attack and Black Panther then

00:04:24.529 --> 00:04:28.610
enters the battle while Shuri attempts to
remove the Mind Stone from Vision.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:32.270
Now, this seems somewhat at odds with the
scene of Corvus Glaive attacking Vision's

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:34.740
Mind Stone with the tip of his blade in the
trailer.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:39.130
So, this could be a moment before then where
Shuri is trying to remove the Infinity Stone

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:41.650
before Corvus Glaive gets hold of it.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:45.669
Alternatively, it might be that Shuri is trying
to remove it because Vision has fallen under

00:04:45.669 --> 00:04:50.249
the control of the Black Order when Corvus
Glaive touched his Mind Stone in this moment

00:04:50.249 --> 00:04:51.249
in the trailer.

00:04:51.249 --> 00:04:57.650
And the final Lego set describes what it calls
"Thanos: The Last Battle" and has Iron Man,

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:00.870
Star-Lord and Gamora going up against the
Mad Titan.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:06.020
The scene appears to take place in space with
Thanos using a huge sword to defend himself.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:09.930
The sword Thanos uses sounds like it might
be a little nod to the Infinity Sword which

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:14.819
appeared on the animated Super Hero Squad
Show or possibly Surtur's Twilight Sword which

00:05:14.819 --> 00:05:16.560
we already saw in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:22.150
OK, so those are the six leaked Lego set and
scene descriptions, but before we assume that

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:26.310
these are 100% guaranteed to happen in the
movie, we need to bear in mind that these

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:31.059
are toy sets which may be playing fast and
loose with aspects of the story in the film.

00:05:31.059 --> 00:05:33.520
Toy sets have sometimes switched characters
around.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:37.330
For example, for Avengers: Age of Ultron,
a toy was released of Captain America on the

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:41.520
motorbike that gets launched from the Avengers
quinjet; whereas in the movie, it was Black

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.710
Widow who was on that motorbike.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:47.710
Even if they aren't all accurate, though,
some of these Lego set descriptions do seem

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:51.949
to match up with the snippets we've seen in
the first Infinity War trailer, and give us

00:05:51.949 --> 00:05:54.740
a bit of a better understanding of what might
be going on.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:59.699
So, what do you think about these potential
action scenes for Avengers: Infinity War?

00:05:59.699 --> 00:06:02.509
And what are you most looking forward to seeing
in the movie?

